    "intro_html":  "Fasolakia is the Greek braise of green beans and potatoes cooked slow in olive oil until everything goes tender and sweet. Traditionally it is a meatless summer dish. We brown turkey into the pot and serve it over rice, which turns a light lunch into a container that actually holds you until dinner. It runs \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
